    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The positive integers $a$ and $b$ satisfy the equation $a^2 + b^2 = 100$. What is the value of $a + b$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "11"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "13"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "14"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Try the squares",
        "body": "The squares below 100 are $1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36, 49, 64, 81$. The only two that add up to 100 are $36 + 64$, so $\\{a, b\\} = \\{6, 8\\}$ and $a + b = 14$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 14**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Scale a Pythagorean triple",
        "body": "$a^2 + b^2 = 10^2$ means $(a, b, 10)$ is a Pythagorean triple; the only one with hypotenuse 10 is $2\\cdot(3, 4, 5) = (6, 8, 10)$. So $a + b = 14$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 14**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "number-theory"
    ],
