    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The figure shows four equilateral triangles and two squares. Each equilateral triangle has two vertices which coincide with the vertices of the inner square, and the third vertex coincides with a vertex of the outer square. The area of the inner square is 1. What is the area of the outer square?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2014-g1112/q27.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$2\\sqrt3$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$2 + \\sqrt3$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$4$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$3 + \\sqrt2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$1 + \\sqrt2 + \\sqrt3$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Half-diagonal of the outer square",
        "body": "The inner square has side 1. Each equilateral triangle stands on one of its sides and points outwards to a corner of the outer square. By symmetry, the centre $O$, the midpoint of an inner side and the opposite triangle apex (an outer corner) lie on one line. The distance from $O$ to an inner side is $\\frac12$ and the height of the triangle is $\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$, so the outer square's half-diagonal is $\\frac{1 + \\sqrt3}{2}$, and its diagonal is $1 + \\sqrt3$.\n\nArea $= \\frac{\\text{diagonal}^2}{2} = \\frac{(1+\\sqrt3)^2}{2} = \\frac{4 + 2\\sqrt3}{2} = 2 + \\sqrt3$.\n\n**Answer: (B)**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Cut into pieces",
        "body": "The outer square consists of the inner square (area 1), the four equilateral triangles (area $\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}$ each, $\\sqrt3$ together) and four more triangles, one along each side of the outer square. Each of these has two sides of length 1 (sides of equilateral triangles) meeting at a vertex of the inner square, with angle $360^\\circ - 90^\\circ - 60^\\circ - 60^\\circ = 150^\\circ$, so its area is $\\frac12\\cdot 1\\cdot 1\\cdot\\sin 150^\\circ = \\frac14$.\n\nTotal: $1 + \\sqrt3 + 4\\cdot\\frac14 = 2 + \\sqrt3$.\n\n**Answer: (B)**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
